 "_comment": [
  "The posting presets, stated once, asserted by BOTH implementations (#107).",
  "postroll/posting_preset.py is the declared source of truth and had no direct",
  "Python tests; only its Swift mirror (PostingPreset) was pinned, so the",
  "declared source could change and only the copy would complain.",
  "",
  "Every case here is checked by tests/test_posting_preset.py and by",
  "PostRollApp/Tests/PostingPresetTests.swift. Adding a case obliges both.",
  "",
  "A null format means the day is NOT governed by the preset (Tuesday,",
  "Thursday, Friday have fixed formats) and the caller uses that day's own",
  "handling. That is different from a day that does not exist.",
  "",
  "`opening` is the third preset (#900). Sunday carries 7, which is the day Dan had 7 photos worth using and the app used 4; Monday and Wednesday stay at 4. A preset governs all three collage days at once, so this cannot say \"Sunday only\" without also declaring what the other two do, which is why they are pinned here rather than left out."
 ],
